But need exactly 6 reactions total, root children list should have first reaction, whose product leads to next etc. However the JSON above lists all reactions as siblings, not nested. The correct hierarchical route: each reaction's product is the parent molecule of next step. So we need nested children: root mol -> reaction1 -> children (precursor1, precursor2). One of those precursors (the aromatic amine) is further broken down by reaction2 etc. So we need nested structure.

Simplify: We'll nest only the amine branch; other branch (sulfonyl chloride) ends there.

Thus:

Root mol children: reaction R1 with two precursors: sulfonyl chloride (mol) and amine (mol). The amine mol has its own child reaction R2 etc.

